      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Another way to check if it\u0027s a directory](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/providers/MediaProvider/src/com/android/providers/media/MediaProvider.java;l\u003d4650-4654;drc\u003de81def57a55a3d03bde7e7a09f3fa9be5e7f495e) (which is actually a place where null is assigned to mime_type too):\n```\n        final Integer formatObject \u003d values.getAsInteger(FileColumns.FORMAT);\n        final int format \u003d formatObject \u003d\u003d null ? 0 : formatObject;\n        if (format \u003d\u003d MtpConstants.FORMAT_ASSOCIATION) {\n            values.putNull(MediaColumns.MIME_TYPE);\n        }\n```\n\n(FORMAT_ASSOCIATION means a directory.)\n\nIf it\u0027s true that mime_type being null is the reason for this issue, and that that\u0027s because a non-directory can have a null mime type, then I am not sure how else to resolve this currently besides checking the FORMAT instead. There *might* not be another way, apart from checking with the underlying filesystem (which is where FUSE has been getting all directory info before this).",
